[issue.1682]
number = 1682
title = "[Coherence] IsHistoricalReplay disagrees with the precompile version selector, so the final part of the v5.7.5 replay range takes the current association path"
revision = "bb8caac8b3e73e3e2f4b330805574f0bcb540641"
verdict = "task"
evidence = "The guard introduced by commit 20a20c0f712758dfa234ebf288364d14bce0ae3f still excludes v6.0.0 at utils/helpers/legacy/v575/associate.go:15 and redirects association and migration at :32 and :47, although sdk/x/upgrade/keeper/keeper.go:303 selects the next completed upgrade and node/app.go:3748 copies that name into tracing contexts, while engine/deps/xevm/keeper/keeper.go:183 and the served selector at modules/evm/keeper/keeper.go:386 select the last version active at the height, leaving the v575 implementation registered by precompiles/addr/setup.go:30 active until v6.0.0, with different account-number, sequence and self-migration results in utils/helpers/associate.go:50 and :69 and only manually named replay contexts in utils/helpers/legacy/v575/repair_m784_test.go:148 and :267."
close_comment = "Historical address association still takes the current migration path for part of the v5.7.5 replay interval because the next upgrade name is mistaken for the selected precompile version. A repair task will bind association and migration replay to the selected version and prove the historical account and balance changes across the v6.0.0 boundary."

